### Programming with R

::: {style="font-size:30px;"}
For doing all these tasks and obtain a efficient and powerful analysis we will need to use a programming language.

-   We will use a **programming language** design for support statistics and data manipulation: [R](https://cran.rstudio.com/)

-   We will need a **development environment** or IDE that allows us to use R and work with it in a better way: [RStudio](https://posit.co/download/rstudio-desktop/)
:::

::: {.callout-note appearance="simple"}
**Installation**

You can go [here](https://rstudio-education.github.io/hopr/starting.html) or see the available guide on canvas.
:::

